# Diagnose Pomegr reporting

Perform a read-only diagnosis. Do not edit files, emit or clear signals, invoke Pomegr tools as connection tests, or expose MCP configuration values.

## Policy

Resolve this plugin's `scripts/policy.mjs` relative to this file and run `node <script> validate --cwd <repository-root>`. Interpret its bounded JSON:

- `valid`: show path, byte size, Session progress state, and `delegatedAgents`. {{#codex}}Version 6 is progress-disabled.{{/codex}}{{#claude}}Report `warnings` as delegation drift and recommend `/pomegr:init` for drift. Version 6 is progress-disabled.{{/claude}}
- `missing`: report repository-specific reporting as inactive and recommend {{#codex}}`$pomegr:init`{{/codex}}{{#claude}}`/pomegr:init`{{/claude}}.
- `invalid`: show the bounded errors and recommend {{#codex}}`$pomegr:init`{{/codex}}{{#claude}}`/pomegr:init`{{/claude}} to review an update.

